  "result": "The bug is fixed: `Cart.remove('sku-1')` now drops the Widget line.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` compared each line's item **name** (`'Widget'`) to the SKU it was given (`'sku-1'`). They never matched, so nothing was removed. `Cart.add` matches on `item.sku`, so `remove` now does the same:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]\n```\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, which is the Gadget line left over. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`: all 6 pass.\n\nNone of the existing tests cover `Cart.remove`, which is how this got through. I can add a short regression test if you'd like.",
